{
  "catalogs": [
    { "user": ".*", "catalog": "iceberg", "allow": "all" },
    { "user": ".*", "catalog": "system", "allow": "read-only" }
  ],
  "schemas": [
    { "user": ".*", "catalog": "iceberg", "schema": ".*", "owner": true }
  ],
  "tables": [
    {
      "_comment": "clinical_user: full access, matching allowed_classifications in governance/phi_classification.yml (PHI, QUASI_PHI, SENSITIVE, PUBLIC, INTERNAL — i.e. everything). Listed explicitly (rather than relying on the fallback rule below) so the mapping from role name to policy is visible here, not just inherited by omission.",
      "user": "clinical_user.*",
      "catalog": "iceberg",
      "schema": ".*",
      "table": ".*",
      "privileges": ["SELECT", "INSERT", "DELETE", "UPDATE", "OWNERSHIP"]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "data_engineer: allowed_classifications = [INTERNAL, SENSITIVE, PUBLIC] — operational/reliability metadata and surrogate keys, but not PHI/QUASI_PHI value columns. Column list mirrors the PHI+QUASI_PHI entries in governance/phi_classification.yml (NOT the SENSITIVE surrogate *_id columns, which data_engineer is allowed to see).",
      "user": "data_engineer.*",
      "catalog": "iceberg",
      "schema": "bronze|silver|quality|icebergdata|deid|gold",
      "table": ".*",
      "privileges": ["SELECT"],
      "columns": [
        { "name": "medical_record_number", "allow": false },
        { "name": "first_name", "allow": false },
        { "name": "last_name", "allow": false },
        { "name": "date_of_birth", "allow": false },
        { "name": "email", "allow": false },
        { "name": "phone", "allow": false },
        { "name": "address_line1", "allow": false },
        { "name": "city", "allow": false },
        { "name": "postal_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "description", "allow": false },
        { "name": "name", "allow": false },
        { "name": "dosage", "allow": false },
        { "name": "value", "allow": false },
        { "name": "result_value", "allow": false },
        { "name": "abnormal_flag", "allow": false },
        { "name": "encounter_start", "allow": false },
        { "name": "encounter_end", "allow": false },
        { "name": "diagnosed_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "performed_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "result_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "observed_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "icd10_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "cpt_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "ndc_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "loinc_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "code", "allow": false }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "analyst / ai_agent: allowed_classifications = [PUBLIC, INTERNAL] only. On top of the data_engineer deny list, also deny the SENSITIVE surrogate-key columns (patient_id, encounter_id, ... and npi) — record_token (INTERNAL, HMAC-keyed, non-reversible; see macros/lineage.sql) is the correlation handle this tier gets instead. Scoped to silver|quality only: bronze/raw are pipeline internals this tier has no business reading directly, and with no matching rule for them the file-based access control's default-deny takes over.",
      "user": "analyst.*|ai_agent.*",
      "catalog": "iceberg",
      "schema": "silver|quality",
      "table": ".*",
      "privileges": ["SELECT"],
      "columns": [
        { "name": "medical_record_number", "allow": false },
        { "name": "first_name", "allow": false },
        { "name": "last_name", "allow": false },
        { "name": "date_of_birth", "allow": false },
        { "name": "email", "allow": false },
        { "name": "phone", "allow": false },
        { "name": "address_line1", "allow": false },
        { "name": "city", "allow": false },
        { "name": "postal_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "description", "allow": false },
        { "name": "name", "allow": false },
        { "name": "dosage", "allow": false },
        { "name": "value", "allow": false },
        { "name": "result_value", "allow": false },
        { "name": "abnormal_flag", "allow": false },
        { "name": "encounter_start", "allow": false },
        { "name": "encounter_end", "allow": false },
        { "name": "diagnosed_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "performed_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "result_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "observed_at", "allow": false },
        { "name": "icd10_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "cpt_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "ndc_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "loinc_code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "code", "allow": false },
        { "name": "patient_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "encounter_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "diagnosis_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "procedure_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "medication_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "lab_result_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "observation_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "provider_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "facility_id", "allow": false },
        { "name": "npi", "allow": false }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "De-identified and aggregate-only schemas are safe for the broad analyst/ai_agent tier as-is (no PHI or SENSITIVE columns exist there in the first place).",
      "user": "analyst.*|ai_agent.*",
      "catalog": "iceberg",
      "schema": "deid|gold",
      "table": ".*",
      "privileges": ["SELECT"]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "Fallback for everyone not matching one of the 4 governed roles above — the demo's own plumbing (dbt's/Metabase's default 'trino'/'admin' users) keeps the full access it already had, so existing flows aren't disturbed. This is a platform-admin/service identity, not a substitute for assigning real interactive users one of the 4 roles above.",
      "user": ".*",
      "catalog": "iceberg",
      "schema": ".*",
      "table": ".*",
      "privileges": ["SELECT", "INSERT", "DELETE", "UPDATE", "OWNERSHIP"]
    }
  ]
}
